  "Verified dataset markets and collective licensing": "ᓈᓚᐅᑎᑕᐅᓯᒪᔪᑦ Dataset ᓂᐅᖅᕿᓂᐊᑦ ᐊᒻᒪᓗ ᑲᑎᑎᑕᐅᔪᒥᒃ License-ᖃᕐᓂᖅ",
  "Verified in both LTR and RTL contexts: the panel mirrors correctly for Arabic and Persian without any special-casing, using logical CSS positioning.": "ᓈᓚᐅᑎᑕᐅᓯᒪᔪᖅ ᒪᕐᕉᔪᓂᒃ LTR RTL contexts-ᒥ: panel ᓈᒻᒪᒋᔭᐅᓂᒃᑯᑦ mirror-ᑐᖅ Arabic Persian-ᒧᑦ ᓱᓇᑐᐃᓐᓇᖅ special-casing ᐱᔭᕆᐊᖃᖅᑎᑕᐅᙱᑎᓪᓗᒍ, logical CSS positioning ᐊᑐᖅᑎᓪᓗᒍ.",
  "Verify": "ᐅᖃᖅᑎᒍᒃ",
  "Version history of this site and its protocol drafts.": "ᐅᓇ Site-ᐅᑉ ᐊᒻᒪᓗ Protocol Draft-ᐃᖏᓐᓄᑦ Version History-ᐊ.",
  "Version history of this site and its protocol drafts. Breaking spec changes are recorded here.": "ᐅᓇ Site-ᐅᑉ ᐊᒻᒪᓗ Protocol Draft-ᐃᖏᓐᓄᑦ Version History-ᐊ. Breaking spec ᐊᓪᓚᖒᑎᑦ ᒫᓂ ᑎᑎᕋᖅᑕᐅᔪᑦ.",
  "Versioned specifications, JSON Schemas, and the policy files actually deployed on this site. Every file can be downloaded, validated, and cited directly.": "Version-ᖃᖅᑎᑕᐅᓯᒪᔪᑦ specification-ᒃᑯᑦ, JSON Schema-ᒃᑯᑦ, ᐊᒻᒪᓗ ᒪᓕᒐᖅ file-ᒃᑯᑦ ᐃᓗᒧᒻᒥ ᐅᓇ site-ᒥ ᐊᑐᓕᖅᑎᑕᐅᓯᒪᔪᑦ. File ᐊᑕᐅᓯᕐᒥᓘᓐᓃᑦ download-ᑕᐅᓯᓐᓇᖅᑐᖅ, validate-ᑕᐅᓯᓐᓇᖅᑐᖅ, ᐊᒻᒪᓗ ᓇᕿᑕᐅᓐᓇᖅᑐᖅ ᐃᓗᒧᒻᒥ.",
  "Versioning": "Version-ᖃᕐᓂᖅ",
  "Versions": "Version-ᒃᑯᑦ",
  "Video and audio companions to the protocols and papers — the AI rights layer, watchable and listenable.": "Video ᓂᐱ ᐃᓚᒋᔭᐅᔪᓪᓗ Protocol-ᒃᑯᓄᑦ ᑎᑎᖅᖃᓄᓪᓗ — AI ᐱᔪᓐᓇᐅᑕᐃ ᐃᓚᖔ, ᑕᑯᔭᐅᓐᓇᖅᑐᖅ ᓈᓚᒃᑕᐅᓐᓇᖅᑐᓪᓗ.",
  "Videos": "Video-ᒃᑯᑦ",
  "Want to generate your own policy file?": "ᓇᒻᒥᓂᖅ ᒪᓕᒐᖅ File ᓴᓇᔪᒪᒋᑦ?",
  "Web fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which receives standard font requests from your browser. No other third-party scripts are used.": "Web font-ᒃᑯᑦ Google Fonts-ᒥᑦ load-ᑕᐅᓯᒪᔪᑦ, ᑕᐃᒫᒃᑯᑦ standard font request-ᒃᑯᓂᒃ ᑎᒍᓯᔪᖅ ᓇᒻᒥᓂᖅ browser-ᑎᑦ. ᐊᓪᓚᑦ third-party script-ᒃᑯᑦ ᐊᑐᖅᑕᐅᙱᑦᑐᑦ.",
  "What AI systems may do with content: read, summarize, transform, retrieve, train, commercialize, redistribute. The AICR ruleset and the AICL licensing layer make these rights declarable and transactable.": "AI-ᒃᑯᑦ ᖃᓄᖅ ᑎᑎᖅᖃᓂᒃ ᐱᓕᕆᖃᔪᓐᓇᖅᒪᖔᑕ: read, summarize, transform, retrieve, train, commercialize, redistribute. AICR ᒪᓕᒐᕐᔪᐊᖏᑦ AICL license-ᖃᕐᓂᕐᒧᑦ ᐃᓚᖔᓂᓪᓗ ᑖᒃᑯᓂᖓ ᐱᔪᓐᓇᐅᑎᓂᒃ ᓇᓗᓇᐃᖅᓯᔪᓐᓇᖅᑎᑦᓯᔪᓐᓇᖅᑎᑦᓯᔪᑦ ᓂᐅᖅᕿᓂᖃᖅᑎᑦᓯᓐᓇᖅᑎᑦᓯᔪᓐᓇᖅᑎᑦᓯᓗᑎᓪᓗ.",
  "What a server can return when an AI crawler requests licensed content without a license token — a machine-actionable quote instead of a dead end.": "ᓱᓇᐅᕝᕙ server-ᒥᒃ ᐅᑎᕐᑎᑦᓯᒍᓐᓂᖅᒪᖔᑕ AI crawler-ᒥᑦ request-ᑕᖅᑎᓪᓗᒍ license-ᖃᖅᑎᑕᐅᓯᒪᔪᒥᒃ ᑎᑎᖅᖃᒥᒃ license token-ᒥᒃ ᐃᓚᐅᙱᑎᓪᓗᒍ — ᖃᕆᐊᓴᒃᑯᑦ ᐱᓕᕆᖃᓱᓐᓇᖅᑎᑕᐅᓯᒪᔪᖅ quote-ᒥᒃ dead end-ᒥᙱᑐᑐᐃᓐᓇᖅ.",
  "What this site is": "ᓱᓇ ᐅᓇ Site",
  "What this site is not": "ᓱᓇ ᐅᓇ Site-ᐃᙳᓂᙱᑦᑐᖅ",
  "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration": "When The Machines Deserve Our Consideration",
  "Whether AI may learn, to what depth, for which purposes, and under what obligations. Being read is not being learned from; \"not prohibited\" is not \"learnable\". AIRS and AILP turn learning permission into a graduated, machine-readable spectrum.": "AI ᐃᓕᓐᓂᐊᖅᑎᑦᓯᓐᓇᖅᐸ, ᖃᓄᖅ ᐃᑎᒐᐃᓇᕐᒥᒃ, ᓱᓇᑐᐃᓐᓇᖅ ᑐᕌᖓᓄᑦ, ᐊᒻᒪᓗ ᓱᓇᒥᒃ ᐱᖁᔭᖅᑕᐅᓪᓗᓂ. Read-ᓂᖃᖅᑐᖅ ᐃᓕᓐᓂᐊᖅᑕᐅᖏᓐᓇᒪ; \"not prohibited\" \"learnable\"-ᐃᙱᑦᑐᖅ. AIRS AILP-ᓗ ᐃᓕᓐᓂᐊᖅᑎᑦᓯᓂᖅ ᐱᔪᓐᓇᐅᑎᖅ ᐊᓪᓚᖑᖅᑎᑦᑐᒃ ᐃᑎᒐᐃᓇᕐᒥᒃ, ᖃᕆᐊᓴᒃᑯᑦ ᐊᑐᖅᑕᐅᔪᓐᓇᖅᑐᒧᑦ ᐃᓚᖏᓪᓗ.",
  "Whitepapers": "Whitepaper-ᒃᑯᑦ",
